{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grdbpersistence"]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"collection","externalID":"GRDBPersistence","modules":[{"name":"GRDBPersistence"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"GRDBPersistence","symbolKind":"module"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RecordStore"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for apps on Apple platforms that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already keep a GRDB database. It takes the app’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseQueue"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabasePool"},{"type":"text","text":" and a table"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name, creates the table with a migration of its own, and opens no second SQLite database. It is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"product of its own, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It makes the same promises as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":". The tracker’s worker commits each record, in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transaction of its own, before publishing it. A batch’s rows are marked before any destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receives it and deleted once every destination has. The table holds at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"type":"text","text":" bytes of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoded records, 5 MiB by default, with the oldest rows deleted to make room, and each drop is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore.dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":". Records are encoded as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" encodes them, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same events are kept: every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" in the program and the library’s own, or only the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" types "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore(events:database:)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists. Rows written by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier, in an earlier encoding, aren’t read: each is deleted when the store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opens and reported as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".undecodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".versionMismatch"},{"type":"text","text":" where its stored version differs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its type’s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"How durable a commit is against power loss is the database’s choice, through its journal mode and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronous"},{"type":"text","text":" setting. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore.synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" checkpoints a database in WAL mode; call it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as the app moves to the background. Open one store per table at a time, and don’t open one from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside an access to the same database."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once a delivered record’s row is deleted, and in WAL mode once a later "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" succeeds,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing of it is left in the database’s main file or its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-wal"},{"type":"text","text":" file. The store’s deletes run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with SQLite’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"secure_delete"},{"type":"text","text":" ON and its inserts with at least FAST, so freed pages and moved rows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are zeroed, and the app’s own setting is put back after each. In WAL mode, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"truncates the log, which until then holds the deleted rows’ earlier bytes. While another"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connection reads or writes the database, such as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabasePool"},{"type":"text","text":" read whose transaction is still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"open, the log can’t be truncated, and the delivered records’ bytes, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" values and session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, stay in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-wal"},{"type":"text","text":" file until a later "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" runs after that connection is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"done. Inside a transaction, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"synchronize()"},{"type":"text","text":" checkpoints nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing is promised outside those two files: a ","type":"text"},{"code":"-journal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the app keeps with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"journal_mode=PERSIST","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can hold earlier rows’ bytes, and the file system may keep the blocks a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"truncated or deleted file gave up. ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s documentation covers how long","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"synchronize()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" waits under each busy mode, and how a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabasePool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" empties the log itself.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app with no database of its own uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":", which needs no GRDB."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import GRDB","import GRDBPersistence","","let database = try DatabaseQueue(path: databasePath)","let store = try DatabaseStore(database: database, table: \"analyticsRecord\")","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what a store keeps, its bounds and recovery."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"API","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"API"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where this module’s API isn’t there, so its symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have no pages of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for an Apple target.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Keeping-records-in-a-database","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Keeping records in a database"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DatabaseStore","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DatabaseStoreError","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"type":"topic","title":"GRDBPersistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/persistingrecords":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Persisting Records"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","title":"Persisting Records","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","type":"link"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","url":"\/documentation\/persistence","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"title":"Persistence","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"}}}